From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a second SIGTERM does not cut a clean exit short

Chromium answers the first SIGTERM, SIGINT or SIGHUP with a graceful
shutdown and puts the default action back, so a second one kills the
browser on the spot. A session end always sends a second: systemd
signals every process in the session's scope, the launcher too, and the
launcher passes its own SIGTERM on to the engine. The browser died part
way through SessionEnding(), before EndSession() wrote the clean-exit
beacon, so every start counted a crash and grew the variations crash
streak.

After the first shutdown signal the browser now ignores all three. The
launcher and systemd still end a hung browser with SIGKILL.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`. guard-clean-exit.sh checks it.
---
 chrome/browser/shutdown_signal_handlers_posix.cc | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/shutdown_signal_handlers_posix.cc b/chrome/browser/shutdown_signal_handlers_posix.cc
index 2fe6adc..1f1ed9f 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/shutdown_signal_handlers_posix.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/shutdown_signal_handlers_posix.cc
@@ -39,10 +39,17 @@ int g_shutdown_pipe_read_fd = -1;
 
 // Common code between SIG{HUP, INT, TERM}Handler.
 void GracefulShutdownHandler(int signal) {
-  // Reinstall the default handler.  We had one shot at graceful shutdown.
+  // Ignore every later shutdown signal. A session end sends more than one:
+  // systemd signals each process in the session, and the launcher that
+  // started this one signals it too. The default action would kill the
+  // browser part way through SessionEnding(), before it records a clean exit,
+  // and the next start would count a crash. A launcher that will not wait
+  // sends SIGKILL.
   struct sigaction action = {};
-  action.sa_handler = SIG_DFL;
-  RAW_CHECK(sigaction(signal, &action, nullptr) == 0);
+  action.sa_handler = SIG_IGN;
+  for (int shutdown_signal : {SIGTERM, SIGINT, SIGHUP}) {
+    RAW_CHECK(sigaction(shutdown_signal, &action, nullptr) == 0);
+  }
 
   RAW_CHECK(g_pipe_pid != -1);
   RAW_CHECK(g_shutdown_pipe_write_fd != -1);
